@@ -0,0 +1,58 @@
+.. SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
+
+Kernel driver qcom-qpt-hwmon
+============================
+
+Supported chips:
+
+  * Qualcomm PMK8850 power telemetry (QPT)
+
+    Prefix: 'qcom_qpt'
+
+Description
+-----------
+
+A PBS (programmable boot sequencer) client of the PMK8850 samples the output
+power of up to 23 switching regulators of the PMICs around it (CPU clusters,
+GPU, NSP, the SoC's CX / MX rails, the DDR and I/O bucks) and adds it up in
+the PMK8850's SDAM blocks. The boot firmware writes the configuration: which
+regulators, the sample timer and the scale of one count. The client copies
+the per-regulator totals into the data SDAM once per report (about once a
+second), with a time stamp. The driver never starts the client by itself:
+the first read of an energy or power attribute starts it, and it is stopped
+again ``idle_ms`` milliseconds after the last such read (module parameter,
+default 10000, 0 = never), at every system suspend and when the driver goes.
+While it is stopped it costs nothing and the energy counters stand still. The
+driver reads the accumulators on demand and does not take the per-report
+interrupt, so the telemetry never wakes the CPUs.
+
+The readings are the output power of each regulator, not its input: the
+regulators' conversion losses, the PMICs themselves, the display backlight
+and everything supplied straight from the battery rail are not in them.
+
+Sysfs entries
+-------------
+
+======================= ===================================================
+energyN_input		Energy delivered by regulator N while the telemetry
+			ran since the driver started, in microjoule. Reading
+			it starts the telemetry.
+energyN_label		Name of the rail (from the device tree, or "s<k><p>"
+			for SMPS k of PMIC p).
+powerN_average		Average output power of regulator N over the reports
+			of the last update interval, in microwatt, from the
+			report time stamps. A window that ended more than two
+			intervals ago is measured again, so the read can take
+			one interval or a little more (two reports after a
+			start). Reading it starts the telemetry.
+powerN_label		As energyN_label.
+update_interval		Length of the averaging window in milliseconds
+			(100 to 10000, default 1000).
+======================= ===================================================
+
+Debugfs
+-------
+
+``qcom_qpt/raw`` shows the configuration bytes, the decoded timer and scale,
+the control and time stamp bytes, the raw accumulators and the driver's
+counters (overflows, re-reads, rejected reads).
